This code uses the pigpio library for GPIO control and I2C communication. It initializes the GPIO and I2C bus, sets up the LED pin for output, and continuously reads pressure and temperature data from the MLX90834 and ADS1115, respectively. If the pressure exceeds 105.0 kPa, it turns on the LED. The code handles I2C errors and retries up to three times before exiting. It also ensures that all resources are properly released when a SIGINT (Ctrl+C) is received.

Before compiling, make sure to install pigpio:

```bash
sudo apt-get install pigpio
```

Compile the code with:

```bash
gcc -o pressure_sensor pressure_sensor.c -lpigpio
```

Then run it:

```bash
./pressure_sensor
```

