This code initializes SPI and the ADC channel, sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and continuously reads the ADC value, logs it to a file, and handles errors appropriately. It cleans up resources on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

Please note that you need to install `libgpiod` and `pigpio` libraries on your Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to compile and run this code. You can install them using the following commands:

```bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install libgpiod-dev pigpio
```

After installing the libraries, compile the code with `gcc -o moisture_logger moisture_logger.c -lgpiod -lpigpio`.

