This code sets up the MCP3008 ADC, reads analog voltage from the Keyes KY-026 Flame Sensor, logs the data, and controls a buzzer on GPIO 18. It handles errors, retries failed reads, and gracefully handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) to stop the sampling loop and turn off the buzzer. The ambient temperature is read from a local file, and the ADC values are temperature-compensated. The program logs the data in a specific format and writes to a log file.

