This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to continuously read a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor using an MCP3008 ADC connected on the SPI bus. It samples the moisture level every 5 seconds, logs readings with timestamps, and controls a 12V water pump through a relay on GPIO17. The program uses hysteresis to turn the pump on when the moisture level falls below 300 and off when it rises above 600. It handles errors gracefully, uses a circular buffer for logging, and ensures proper resource cleanup on exit. The program runs in an infinite loop until interrupted by SIGINT or SIGTERM.

