This code sets up an I2C communication with the MAX30102 sensor on Raspberry Pi's I2C bus 1. It checks for the sensor's presence by reading the Part ID register and logs any errors to stderr and a file named `health_log.txt`. It continuously samples the SpO₂ and heart-rate values, writing any readings below 95% or above 100 BPM to the log file. The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) and SIGTERM signals by releasing the I2C handle and any driver resources before exiting.

Please note that this code assumes the `pigpio` library is installed and available. If not, you'll need to install it using `sudo apt-get install pigpio`. Also, ensure that the necessary permissions are set for the I2C device.

