This code sets up a continuous monitoring system for a Honeywell SS49E linear Hall-effect sensor connected to an ADS1115 ADC via I2C. It samples the ADC at 1 Hz, converts the voltage readings to magnetic field strength, maintains a rolling average in a circular buffer, and triggers a GPIO27 HIGH output when the threshold (500 Gauss) is exceeded. The program logs errors and warnings via syslog, handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, and ensures proper resource cleanup.

Please note that you need to install pigpio library and have the necessary permissions to access I2C and GPIO pins. Also, this code assumes that the ADS1115 is properly configured and powered.

