This code initializes the SPI and GPIO interfaces, calibrates the ambient noise level, continuously samples sound levels, and toggles an LED when the sound level exceeds a threshold with a 10ms debounce. It handles errors and performs graceful cleanup on SIGINT.

Please note that this code assumes the Adafruit MAX9814 Electret Microphone Amplifier is connected to the MCP3008 ADC correctly and the LED is connected to GPIO17. Also, ensure that the necessary libraries (libgpiod or pigpio) are installed and configured correctly.

To compile this code, use the following command:

```bash
gcc -o sound_level_monitor sound_level_monitor.c -lwiringPi -lspidev
```

