This code snippet captures MJPEG video frames from a USB webcam connected to /dev/video0, writes timestamps to frame_log.txt, and handles errors at every step. It uses select() for asynchronous I/O to avoid blocking and memory-maps the video frames for efficient access. The program gracefully shuts down on SIGINT (Ctrl+C) and releases all resources before exiting.

Please note that this code assumes the MJPEG format is correctly handled by the webcam driver. It does not include specific MJPEG decoding logic, as the driver is expected to provide the frames in the correct format.

Before compiling, ensure you have the necessary libraries installed:

```sh
sudo apt-get install libv4l-dev libjpeg-dev libpng-dev
```

Compile the code with:

```sh
gcc -o mjpeg_capture mjpeg_capture.c -lv4l2 -ljpeg -lpng
```

Run the program with:

```sh
sudo ./mjpeg_capture
```

To stop the program, press Ctrl+C.

