This code sets up a PWM for controlling a camera pan-tilt mount using GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi. It also listens for button presses on four active-low push buttons connected to the GPIO pins. The program initializes both servos to the mid-position value (75) and adjusts the corresponding axis by ±5 while clamping the position to the range 25–125 on each button press. It polls the button states every 50 milliseconds and handles any request failures. Upon receiving a SIGINT (Ctrl+C), it cleansly releases all allocated resources.

