This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to measure water flow rate using a YF-S201 sensor connected to GPIO17 and an LCD1602 connected via I2C. It reads pulses from the sensor over a 1-second interval, calculates the flow rate in liters per minute, and displays the result on the LCD. The program includes error handling for GPIO and I2C initialization, pulse reading, and sensor absence detection. It also cleans up resources on exit and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for a graceful shutdown.

Please note that this code assumes a 1-to-1 relationship between pulses and liters for simplicity. In a real-world scenario, you might need to calibrate the sensor to get accurate flow rate measurements. Also, the I2C address and LCD pin configuration might need adjustments based on your hardware setup.

