This code sets up GPIO pins for reading from an IR sensor (active-low) and controlling a buzzer (active-high) on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It logs each state transition to a file named `obstacle_log.txt` with an ISO 8601 timestamp. The program polls the sensor every 100ms and handles errors rigorously, including chip open failures, line request failures, and read/write errors. It also includes signal handlers for SIGINT (Ctrl+C) and SIGTERM to perform a graceful shutdown, releasing all GPIO lines and closing the chip.

