This code sets up an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor to measure distance and a PWM-driven speaker to produce a theremin-like sound. The distance is mapped to a frequency between 200 Hz and 2000 Hz using a logarithmic scale. The program runs in an infinite loop, continuously reading distance and generating tones. It also includes error checking and a clean exit handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

Please note that this code assumes the use of the `libgpiod` library for GPIO control and the `rtc` library for time management. You'll need to install these libraries before compiling the code.

To compile the code, use the following command:

```bash
gcc -o theremin theremin.c -lgpiod -lrtc
```

This will produce an executable named `theremin`.

