This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to continuously measure distance using an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor connected to GPIO4 (trigger) and GPIO17 (echo), and control a SG90 servo motor connected to GPIO18 based on the distance. The program updates the servo angle every 100ms and displays the distance in centimeters on the console. It also handles echo timeouts and sensor errors, and cleansly exits on SIGINT (Ctrl+C) interruption. The code uses the pigpio library for GPIO control and signal handling.

