This code uses the I2C library (libgpiod or pigpio) for Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to communicate with the Si7021 sensor. It reads the temperature every 2 seconds, buffers the readings in a circular buffer, and prints them to stdout. The fan connected to GPIO18 (active-high) is controlled with hysteresis, turning on when the temperature exceeds 28.0°C and turning off when it falls below 27.0°C. The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by turning off the fan, closing the I2C handle, and invoking the library's call() function before exiting.

