This code uses the pigpio library for I2C communication and handles errors, retries on communication failures, and logs measurements to a file. It runs in an infinite loop, sampling data every second. The first two samples after power-up are skipped due to potential stale data. The program cleans up resources on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

Please note that you need to install pigpio on your Raspberry Pi before compiling and running this code. You can install it via:

```bash
sudo apt-get install pigpio
```

Also, ensure that the Honeywell HAFUHH0025PA3 flow sensor is connected to the Raspberry Pi's I2C bus (usually SDA and SCL on GPIO headers).

