This code reads temperature from an STTS2004 sensor on I2C bus, logs the temperature to stdout once per second, and controls an LED connected to GPIO17 (BCM) with hysteresis. It checks the result of every I2C read and every GPIO operation, logs errno details on repeated I2C failures, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by releasing all driver library resources, turning off the LED, and then exiting cleanly.

Please note that this code assumes the existence of `fctl` and `LED_MODE` macros for setting up the LED, which should be defined according to your hardware setup. Also, the STTS2004 sensor's I2C address (0x40) and the GPIO number (17) are hardcoded and should be adjusted if they differ in your setup.

Before compiling, make sure to install the necessary libraries:

```sh
sudo apt-get install libi2c-dev
```

Compile the code with:

```sh
gcc -o temperature_control temperature_control.c -li2c
```

