This code snippet is a complete C program for a Raspberry Pi 4B that reads temperature from a TMP117, humidity from an AHT20, and motion detection from a PIR sensor, logging the values to daily timestamped CSV files. It uses pigpio for GPIO control and I2C communication. The program samples every 1 second, retries I2C reads up to three times with a 10 ms backoff on failure, creates a new log file at midnight each day, handles I2C errors, and ensures all resources are cleanly released on every exit path, including SIGINT and SIGTERM.

Please note that you need to define `tmp117_reg_addr` and `aht20_reg_addr` with the correct I2C register addresses for your specific TMP117 and AHT20 devices. Also, ensure that the PIR sensor is wired correctly to GPIO 4.

To compile the code, use the command:

```bash
gcc -o logger logger.c -lgpiod -lrt
```

This assumes you have pigpio library installed on your Raspberry Pi. If not, you can install it using:

```bash
sudo apt-get install pigpio
```

