This code uses pigpio for GPIO control and handles all the specified requirements:

- It continuously monitors the YL-83 rain sensor connected to GPIO17.
- It polls the sensor every 2 seconds.
- When rain is detected, it commands the L298N motor driver to close a window by driving the motor forward for exactly 5 seconds.
- Each detection, motor start, motor stop, and any error condition are logged to stdout with a timestamp.
- It checks the return status of every pigpio call and explicitly handles the situation where the GPIO chip cannot be opened.
- It installs SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers to safely stop the motor and release all GPIO lines on program termination.
- It deliberately excludes any DHT22 or humidity sensing functionality.

