This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to communicate with a BMP180 sensor via I2C, configures GPIO2 as a falling-edge interrupt, and toggles data logging every second. It reads the sensor data (temperature and pressure) with oversampling (OSS=3), appends the data to a CSV file, and handles errors gracefully. The program exits gracefully on SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by closing the I2C handle, log file, and releasing the GPIO.

