This code provides a basic framework for interfacing with the ADPD144RI sensor on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using I2C. It includes error handling, logging, and a separate thread for LED control. The main function runs in an infinite loop, sampling the sensor every 100ms and logging the readings to a CSV file. The program also monitors the infrared reading and activates an LED whenever it exceeds a threshold. It handles I2C errors and sensor absence gracefully, and cleans up resources on exit.

