            fprintf(stderr, "Failed to write to log file\n");
        }

        // Flush and close the log file after each write
        if (fflush(i2c_fd) < 0) {
            perror("fflush");
        }

        // Sleep before the next reading
        usleep(READ_INTERVAL * 1000);
    }

    // Clean up and exit
    close(i2c_fd);
    close(log_fd);
    pigpio_terminate(1000);

    return 0;
}
```

This code uses the pigpio library for I2C communication and standard C libraries for file I/O and error handling. It continuously reads data from the Sensirion SLF3S-4000B Liquid Flow Sensor, validates the CRC, converts the raw value to flow rate, logs the measurement to a CSV file, and handles errors appropriately. The program cleans up resources on SIGINT and exits cleanly.

Before compiling, make sure to install pigpio:

```sh
sudo apt-get install pigpio
```

Compile the code with:

```sh
gcc -o flow_monitor flow_monitor.c -lpigpio
```

Run the program with:

```sh
sudo ./flow_monitor
```

