This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interface with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO pins. It continuously monitors two IR sensors connected to GPIO17 and GPIO18. A stall is confirmed when both sensors read LOW for at least 2 seconds. Each stall event is timestamped and logged to `stall_log.txt`, avoiding duplicate entries. The program handles signal interrupts (SIGINT and SIGTERM) to cleanly release resources before exiting.

