This code sets up a Raspberry Pi daemon that continuously polls a digital input pin (GPIO23) connected to a SEN0193 Water Level Sensor. It uses the libgpiod library for GPIO control. The program reads the sensor every 2 seconds, detects a logic HIGH (indicating water), prints an alert message to stdout, and appends a timestamped alert to a log file named `flood_log.txt`.

The daemon handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) and SIGTERM signals, cleans up resources, and exits gracefully. If a GPIO read fails, it logs an error message to the log file and attempts to re-initialize after 60 seconds.

Before compiling, ensure you have the libgpiod library installed on your Raspberry Pi. You can install it using:

```
sudo apt-get install libgpiod-dev
```

Compile the code with:

```
gcc -o water_level_monitor water_level_monitor.c -lgpiod
```

Then, run it as a daemon:

```
sudo ./water_level_monitor &
```

To stop the daemon, use `killall water_level_monitor`.

