This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to monitor a SainSmart TTP223B touch sensor connected to GPIO23 (physical pin 16, BCM 23) and drive an LED on GPIO18 (physical pin 12, BCM 18) with a current-limiting resistor. It polls the sensor every 50ms, illuminating the LED only when the sensor is actively touched. The program uses the `libgpiod` library for GPIO control, logs events and errors to the system syslog, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful shutdown.

