This code uses libpigpio for GPIO control and standard C I/O functions for file handling. It sets up a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM to release GPIO resources and close the log file before exiting. The program continuously polls GPIO4 with a pull-down bias and a debounce interval of 50ms, logging touch events to "touch_log.txt" in the specified format.

Please note that you need to install libpigpio on your Raspberry Pi before compiling this code. You can install it using:

```bash
sudo apt-get install libpigpio-dev
```

Compile the code with:

```bash
gcc -o touch_log touch_log.c -lpigpio
```

Then run the program:

```bash
./touch_log
```

This code assumes that the TTP223 capacitive touch sensor is connected to GPIO4 (physical pin 7) and that the Raspberry Pi's clock is set to provide a high resolution timer (e.g., using `rpi-uptime` to set the time). If the time resolution is not sufficient, you may need to adjust the debounce interval or use a different method to measure time.

