The code includes error handling for I2C communication, retries I2C operations up to three times with a 100ms delay between attempts, and logs errors if all retries fail. It also installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to gracefully release the GPIO line, close the I2C file descriptor, and turn off the LED strip before exiting.

Please note that this code assumes the Raspberry Pi is running a Linux kernel with I2C and GPIO support. Also, the GPIO pin number (18) and I2C bus number (1) might need to be adjusted based on your specific Raspberry Pi setup.

