Please note that this code assumes the existence of a driver library interface at `/sys/kernel/mpu6050_accel/latest` to make the most recent buffered sample available. You may need to implement or adapt this part according to your specific use case.

Also, this code uses epoll for handling I2C data, which is a more modern approach than using POSIX timers. The epoll_create1 function is used to create a new epoll instance, and epoll_ctl is used to add the file descriptor of the I2C device to the epoll instance. The epoll_wait function is used to wait for events on the file descriptor.

Before compiling, make sure to install the necessary libraries:

```sh
sudo apt-get install libi2c-dev libepoll-dev
```

Compile the code with:

```sh
gcc -o mpu6050_accel mpu6050_accel.c -lpthread -lrt -li2c-dev
```

