This code uses libpigpio to control the L293D H-bridge driver and read button inputs. It configures the GPIOs as required, initializes the driver, and implements the full-step two-phase drive with the specified inter-step delay. The program responds to LOCK and UNLOCK button presses by rotating the stepper motor 512 steps in the respective direction, providing console feedback for each event. It also handles driver initialization failure, checks all GPIO configuration return codes, prevents re-triggering while a button remains held, and ensures clean de-energization and resource release on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

