This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to continuously read edge events from a SW-420 vibration sensor connected to GPIO17. It uses libgpiod for GPIO control and epoll for efficient event handling. The program maintains a sliding window of the last five events, logs them to a file with ISO-8601 timestamps, and prints an "EARTHQUAKE ALERT" message when three or more consecutive HIGH events are detected. It handles command-line arguments for poll timeout, logs errors, and cleans up resources on exit. The main loop is interrupted by SIGINT (Ctrl+C) or SIGTERM signals, allowing for a clean shutdown.

