This code uses `pigpio` for GPIO control and `json-c` for logging. It initializes GPIOs, sets up a software debounce mechanism, and toggles a relay upon touch detection. It logs state changes to `relay_log.json` and handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) to toggle the relay OFF before exiting.

To compile this code, you'll need to have `pigpio` and `json-c` libraries installed on your Raspberry Pi. You can compile it using:

```bash
gcc -o relay_monitor relay_monitor.c -lpigpio -ljson-c
```

Make sure to replace `relay_monitor.c` with the actual filename of your source code.

