This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to read the X-axis angular rate from an ADXRS290 gyroscope using hardware SPI0. It uses the `spidev` library for SPI communication and `pthread` for thread-safe access to the circular buffer. The program continuously reads the gyroscope data, timestamps each reading, and stores it in a circular buffer. If the measured rate exceeds 20.0 deg/s, it turns on a warning LED. The program exits gracefully on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, closing the SPI interface, turning off the LED, and releasing all resources.

