This code initializes the MPR121 capacitive touch controller on I2C bus 1, reads touch status every 10 ms, debounces touch events with a 100 ms delay, toggles a 5V relay connected to GPIO17 each time electrode 0 is touched, initializes GPIO17 to a default LOW state, checks every initialization step and every I2C operation for errors, logs all I2C, GPIO, and configuration errors with timestamps to a file named `touch_relay.log`, and on any failure logs the error and exits gracefully. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to cleanly close the I2C interface, release the GPIO pin, and close the log file.

Please note that this code assumes the necessary libraries (libgpiod or pigpio) are already installed and configured on your Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. If you're using wiringPi, you'll need to replace the I2C and GPIO handling code accordingly.

