This code sets up a Raspberry Pi program to continuously monitor a Keyes KY-033 IR Obstacle Avoidance Sensor connected to GPIO 17. It debounces the input by enforcing a minimum interval of 200ms between successive triggers. When a valid trigger occurs, it starts a 5-second video capture using raspivid, saving the file under /home/pi/videos/ with a filename based on the current timestamp in the form YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.h264, and appends a line to /home/pi/logs/motion_log.txt containing an ISO 8601 timestamp for the motion event. It verifies that the sensor driver is successfully initialized, checks that all file operations succeed, and confirms that the system command for video capture executes without error. The program installs a SIGINT handler that, on interruption, cleanly releases all resources by closing the log file and terminating the driver before exiting, allowing the program to run indefinitely until the user stops it.

