This code sets up a Raspberry Pi to monitor a rain sensor and control a DC motor window actuator. It uses the pigpio library for GPIO control, syslog for logging, and handles errors and graceful shutdown. The program polls the rain sensor every 200ms and starts the motor close sequence when it detects a rising edge (dry-to-wet transition). It ensures the motor stays off for at least three consecutive dry readings before re-starting the sequence. The program logs all significant events and exits cleanly on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

