This code uses the pigpio library for GPIO control and the standard C library for file operations and signal handling. It initializes pigpio, sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and continuously monitors the PIR sensor. Upon detecting motion, it activates the relay to turn on the floodlight, logs the event with an ISO-8601 timestamp, waits for 60 seconds, then turns off the floodlight and logs the deactivation event. The program ensures proper error checking and resource cleanup on all exit paths.

