This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to monitor ambient light using a BH1750 sensor connected to I2C bus 1 and control a 12V LED strip via a relay connected to GPIO 17. It logs readings and relay state changes to a file named `chicken_coop_log.txt` with the specified format. The program activates the relay at dusk (lux < 50) and deactivates it at dawn (lux > 200) with hysteresis. It includes comprehensive error handling for driver initialization, I2C communication, and file I/O, ensuring that all resources are released on every exit path, including graceful shutdown when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

