This code initializes pigpio, sets up GPIO pins for input (sensor) and output (relay), and enters a main loop that reads the sensor state. If the state changes, it debounces the input for 50ms, then toggles the relay state if the sensor reads HIGH both before and after the debounce delay. Each relay state change is logged with an ISO-8601 timestamp. The program exits gracefully on SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by turning off the relay, releasing pigpio resources, and printing an exit message.

