This code sets up a Raspberry Pi program to monitor a YF-S201 water flow sensor connected to GPIO 17 (BCM 11) and control a solenoid valve on GPIO 27 (BCM 27). It implements a 1-second ISR debounce timeout on the flow-sensor pin and samples the pulse count every second. The program uses a pthread mutex to protect the shared pulse counter, logs each liters-per-minute (LPM) reading and every solenoid state change with timestamps to a file named `water_flow.log`, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by logging the event, returning the solenoid to its safe open state, closing the log file, destroying the mutex, and calling the library's cleanup API.

Please ensure that the necessary libraries (libgpiod and pigpio) are installed on your Raspberry Pi before compiling and running this code.

