This code sets up a closed-loop proportional solenoid valve control system using a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It uses the pigpio library for hardware PWM and interrupt-driven pulse counting. The valve is connected to GPIO 18, the enable/direction line to GPIO 23, and the flow sensor to GPIO 24. The target flow rate is supplied as a command-line argument, and the program logs the timestamp, flow rate, and valve position every 100ms. The program handles initialization errors, signal handling, and graceful shutdown.

Before compiling, make sure to install the pigpio library:

```sh
sudo apt-get install pigpio
```

Compile the code with:

```sh
gcc -o flow_control flow_control.c -lpigpio -lm
```

