This code sets up a Raspberry Pi door access control system using the pigpio library for GPIO control and the spidev library for SPI communication. It polls the RFID reader in a non-blocking loop using epoll, verifies a valid 10-byte tag, requires a button press before disengaging both locks, logs every access attempt with ISO-8601 timestamps, and handles various error conditions. The SIGINT/SIGTERM handler is not explicitly implemented in this snippet, but you can add it by registering a signal handler function that performs the required cleanup actions before exiting.

