This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to continuously monitor an MPR121 capacitive touch sensor on I2C bus 1. It reads the touch status of all twelve electrodes every 50ms and drives a relay connected to GPIO 17 (BCM) based on the touched electrodes. Any change in the relay state is appended with a timestamp to a text file named `relay_log.txt`. The program includes a robust initialization sequence for the MPR121 sensor, error handling for all operations, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including handling a SIGINT (Ctrl+C) signal to shut down the relay and close any I2C handles properly.

Please note that you need to install `pigpio` library to run this code. You can install it using:

```
sudo apt-get install pigpio
```

Also, ensure that the GPIO 17 is correctly configured as an output in your Raspberry Pi configuration.

