This code uses the libgpiod library to interface with the GPIO pins. It sets up a single-threaded, non-blocking polling loop with a 50ms interval to detect a rising edge from 0 to 1 on GPIO 17 (PIR sensor). Upon detecting motion, it activates the relay on GPIO 18 (door strike relay) for 500ms, then enforces a 2-second rate limit before allowing further events. It logs timestamps and events to a file named `door_events.log`. The program handles errors, cleans up resources on exit, and responds to SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by closing the log file, terminating the driver library, and ensuring the relay is set to off.

