This code sets up a Raspberry Pi program to monitor a weight-triggered solenoid lock using an HX711 load cell amplifier. It reads the HX711 sensor every 500ms, enforces a read timeout of 0.5 seconds, and skips iterations where the timeout occurs. The program initializes the GPIO driver with error checking, loads calibration data from a `calibration.txt` file, performs a one-time startup calibration, computes weight using the loaded or default scale and offset, engages the solenoid when the computed weight exceeds a calibrated threshold of 10.0 kg, logs each reading with a timestamp to `weight_log.txt`, and writes any updated calibration values back to `calibration.txt`. The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) to cleanly shut down by releasing all GPIO resources and closing open files.

