To compile this code, you'll need to install libpiod and ZeroMQ on your Raspberry Pi. You can install libpiod using:

```bash
sudo apt-get install libpiod-dev
```

And ZeroMQ using:

```bash
sudo apt-get install libzmq3-dev
```

Then compile the code with:

```bash
gcc -o sound_alarm sound_alarm.c -lgpiod -lZeroMQ
```

You can run the program with different modes by providing the command-line argument:

```bash
./sound_alarm sound_sensor_mode
```

or

```bash
./sound_alarm alarm_node_mode
```

