This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to continuously read ambient light from a BH1750 sensor connected via I2C, converts the raw value to lux, and broadcasts it as a floating-point string via UDP multicast to 239.255.255.250:5000 with a TTL of 1. It checks for I2C write and read failures, handles errors, and implements signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to cleanly exit. The program runs indefinitely until interrupted.

