This code sets up a UART connection to the Texas Instruments AWR1642 radar sensor, reads data at 115200 baud, 8N1, with a 0.5-second inter-byte timeout and a 2-second select() timeout for detecting sensor-absent or bus-error conditions. It accumulates partial reads into a line buffer, parses complete newline-terminated ASCII lines, and outputs each valid detection as "Timestamp: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS, Range: X.XX meters". The program checks the result of every system call and prints errno-based diagnostics on failure, and installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to ensure a graceful shutdown.

